#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""Zerto Monitor appliance: the console menu's root operations.

Reached only through sudo, from the menu (/usr/local/bin/zerto-monitor-console):

    %zmconsole ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/zerto-monitor-console-ops

It is deliberately NOT part of zerto-monitor-admin, the web app's socket-activated
helper: a compromised web app must not be able to re-IP the box, grow its disk, reset
passwords or apply an upgrade. The app's account (zertomon) is not in zmconsole, and its
unit sets NoNewPrivileges, which stops sudo outright.

Rules: a fixed list of verbs; every argument is validated HERE (the menu's own checks
are a convenience, not the boundary); commands are argument lists, never a shell;
secrets arrive on stdin only. Actions are logged to /var/log/zerto-monitor-console.log
(root, 0600) without secrets.

firstboot.py and the menu import this file (without running it) for the netplan
validation and rendering, so those rules exist exactly once.
"""
